  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What is the linear transformation $T$ whose standard matrix is $T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n| $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\u27f6\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Consider a general vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}].$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+4z \\\\ 5x+3y-2z \\\\ x-6y+7z\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,T\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+4z \\\\ 5x+3y-2z \\\\ x-6y+7z\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
